    "Disconnection fruit: cessation through deliberation.",
    "Retribution fruit: the fruit produced by a retribution cause.",
    "Dominant fruit: the fruit produced by an efficient cause.",
    "An efficient cause need not have a fruit; if it has one, it is a dominant fruit.",
    "Uniform fruit: the fruit produced by homogeneous and universal causes.",
    "Virile fruit: the fruit produced by co-existent and associated causes.",
    "The fruit produced by an immediately contiguous condition is a virile fruit (and may also be a uniform or dominant fruit), because the immediately contiguous condition is [also] a co-existent and associated cause. Virile fruits are of four kinds: co-arisen, immediate, separated, and non-arising. Co-existent and associated causes are mutually co-arisen virile fruits; what is produced by an immediately contiguous condition is an immediate virile fruit; a separated virile fruit is produced through a chain of causal force; the non-arising virile fruit is cessation through deliberation.",
